  "readmeFile": "nuget_readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "11.0.0\n\n* New: a net11.0 build, for .NET 11. The netstandard2.0, net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 builds stay,\n  so nothing changes for a project on an earlier .NET. The major version is 11 because it follows\n  the .NET generation. Nothing was removed or renamed: code that builds against 10.2.1 builds\n  against 11.0.0 as it is.\n* New: SFtpClient.HostKeyFingerprint, which is optional. Set it to the server's host key\n  fingerprint (\"SHA256:...\") and the client refuses a server that shows another key, before the\n  login is sent, with an SshConnectionException that names both fingerprints. Left unset, any host\n  key is accepted, as before. SFtpClient.ServerHostKeyFingerprint holds the fingerprint the server\n  showed, so a caller can trust a server on the first connection and hold it to that key afterwards.\n* Fixed: SFtpFileInfo.Size was always zero. ListFiles, GetFileInfo and their async versions now\n  fill it in.\n* Faster: an upload into a folder that exists asks the server about that folder only, one request\n  whatever the depth. Before, Upload and UploadAsync asked about every folder above the file, from\n  the top, on every call.\n* Readme: a private key in OpenSSH's own format (what ssh-keygen writes) works as it is. The readme\n  said it had to be converted to PEM.\n\n10.2.1 fixed two uploads into the same new remote folder at once making one of them fail:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H.Net.Ssh/10.2.1#releasenotes-body-tab\n\n10.2.0 added SFtpClient.Rename and RenameAsync, and raised the dependency floors to 10.0.13:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H.Net.Ssh/10.2.0#releasenotes-body-tab\n\nUpgrading from 10.0.x or 2.x? 10.1.0 merged the netstandard2.0 and net8.0+ packages into one and\nraised the dependency floors (including SSH.NET 2026.0.0). Its notes list every change:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H.Net.Ssh/10.1.0#releasenotes-body-tab",
